    {
      "claim": "L6 metabolic-stability records for the related NS5A inhibitor M06 report hepatic extraction <12.7% in human microsomes and <12.7%/<9.2% in cynomolgus/rat microsomes, indicating low hepatic first-pass loss for this carbamate-proline-imidazole class.",
      "card_ids": ["C237", "C239", "C267"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The closest query-core analog M07/JNJ-56914845 is primarily metabolized by CYP3A4 (C233), but this is a pathway identification without an extraction ratio; the same compound showed substantial oral AUC0-24 of 7747 ng·h/mL at 60 mg (C122).",
      "card_ids": ["C233", "C122"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Direct human F values for related proline-amide/heteroaromatic scaffolds are at or above the 20% threshold: AZD0837 22–55% (C01), acalabrutinib ~25% (C02), compound 5 41% (C07), MMV367 90% (C23/C26).",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C02", "C07", "C23", "C26"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "P-gp efflux does not preclude F≥20%: maraviroc has a Caco-2 efflux ratio of 3.0 and human F of 33% (C213/C205/C182/C05/C06).",
      "card_ids": ["C213", "C205", "C182", "C05", "C06"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C233", "C237", "C239", "C267"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute F measurement exists for the query molecule or an exact structural match.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability measurement is available; L6 records are for related NS5A inhibitors with different linkers/proline modifications.",
    "The M07 CYP3A4 metabolism record lacks an extraction ratio and an IV comparison, so F cannot be derived from it.",
    "The query's very high MW (738.9) and TPSA (174.6) exceed most reference molecules, limiting transferability of positive records.",
    "Formulation, food effects, and dose-dependent saturation of efflux/metabolism were not assessed for the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L6 adds low hepatic extraction (<12.7% human) for a related NS5A inhibitor and CYP3A4 pathway for the closest analog; neither provides affirmative evidence for F<20%. Combined with direct human F≥20% for related scaffolds and substantial oral exposure for the closest analog, high remains better supported. Confidence moderate due to structural differences and lack of query-specific F."
}

